The suppression mechanism is resolved. compression_decile and IV_ATM_var show weak raw correlation (pooled Pearson r = -0.0177; per-date mean r = -0.0245, src/68 and src/69) but a partial correlation of -0.1220 - roughly 7x larger in magnitude - once both are residualized against the other 9 benchmark features (src/69). This confirms the two variables share variance THROUGH the other 9 features rather than directly with each other: a classic suppression pattern, where two variables with low direct correlation can still substantially move each other's estimated coefficients once correlated common controls are conditioned on. This is consistent with, and explains, the leave-one-out sensitivity already observed (src/67): removing IV_ATM_var from the benchmark set materially increased compression's apparent NW t-stat (from -9.3978 to -13.4303) precisely because IV_ATM_var, in combination with the other 9 controls, was absorbing part of compression's apparent predictive content rather than that content being compression's alone.


